      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ANOTHER WOODS (5) looked good in a resuming with a head win over 2195m at Ararat, where he was sent out favourite and scored in NR 50 to 55 company. He has already won at his only Mt Gambier start and has two wins from six attempts at the distance, so he looks the most reliable winning option. IMAGINATION ORO (4) was only beaten three and a half metres at St Arnaud after being tightened for room and brings a solid longer-distance profile, though her manners remain the watch. EASTBRO KAZ (3) drops out of Saturday Melton company, where the 1:54.5 mile rate gives the run merit, but the 2190m record is the query. WOW YOU CAN DANCE (6) was close up at Melton last week and is a genuine danger for the minors.",
